Details of parsing outbox:
```
def iter_events(path):
    text = path.read_text(errors='replace')
    # whole-file JSON
    try: doc=json.loads(text)
    except: doc=None
    if isinstance(doc,dict): yield doc; return
    if isinstance(doc,list): yield from [d for d in doc if isinstance(d,dict)]; return
    # fenced
    for block in re.findall(r"```(?:json)?\s*(.*?)```", text, re.S):
        ...
    # lines
    for line in text.splitlines():
        line=line.strip().rstrip(',')
        if line.startswith('{') and line.endswith('}'):
            try: yield json.loads(line)
            except: pass
```
Careful: whole-file json.loads on a big JSONL file fails fast; then line mode works. Markdown fenced blocks handled; plus the last part of comms.py also splits lines. Duplicates possible when a fenced block's inner line is also a line; dedupe by event_id.

